{"rules":[{"jurisdiction":"NJ","level":"state","category":"just_cause_eviction","status":"in_force","title":"New Jersey Anti-Eviction Act (good cause eviction)","requirement":"A landlord may recover possession of a residential unit only by tenant consent or court eviction process, and must have statutory good cause to evict or fail to renew a lease. Each cause except nonpayment must be described in detail in a written notice. A Notice to Quit is required for all good cause evictions except nonpayment of rent, and a Notice to Cease is required for some causes. Notice to Quit periods: 3 days for disorderly conduct, property damage, employment-based tenancy and drug or assault convictions; 1 month for rule or lease covenant violations, failure to pay a rent increase, habitual late payment and refusal of lease changes; 2 months for owner occupation or sale after condominium or cooperative conversion; 3 months for health and safety violations or removal from the rental market; 18 months to permanently retire the property from residential use; 3 years for conversion to condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership. Relocation assistance: a tenant evicted for illegal occupancy (G 3) is entitled to six times monthly rent, paid by the landlord. If it is not paid at least 5 days before removal, it may be paid from a municipal relocation fund, or interest accrues at 18% per year and the amount is a lien on the property. Tenants evicted for health and safety or removal-from-market causes may not be evicted until relocation assistance is provided. Self-help evictions and lockouts are illegal. Failure to pay a rent increase is a cause only if the increase is not unconscionable and complies with other laws and municipal ordinances, including rent control.","key_value":"Good cause required; notice to quit 3 days to 3 years depending on cause; relocation assistance of 6x monthly rent for illegal-occupancy evictions","coverage_conditions":"Applies to most residential rental properties, including single-family homes, mobile homes and mobile home park land, apartment buildings and complexes, and rooming and boarding homes.","exemptions":"May not apply to two- or three-unit owner-occupied premises with two or fewer rental units. Does not apply to hotel or motel guests or guest houses rented to transient or seasonal guests (hotel and motel occupants with no alternate residence who reside there continually are covered). Does not apply to a unit held in trust for a developmentally disabled immediate family member who permanently occupies it.","coverage_logic":{"covers":null,"exempt":{"all":[{"field":"units","op":"<=","value":3},{"field":"owner_occupied","op":"==","value":true}]}},"subject":"landlord","interaction":null,"yields_to_local":false,"preempts_local":false,"effective_date":null,"effective_rule":null,"enacted_date":null,"end_date":null,"penalty":"Self-help eviction or unlawful entry makes the landlord liable for damages, including court costs and reasonable attorney fees, and possible disorderly conduct charges.","citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1 et seq.","quoted_span":"A landlord must have good cause to evict a tenant (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-53). There are several grounds for a good cause eviction.","supporting_spans":["This law may not apply to two - or three-unit owner-occupied premises with two (2) or fewer rental units.","Any tenant evicted under G 3) (illegal occupancy) is entitled to relocation assistance in an amount equal to six times the tenant’s monthly rent."],"confidence":0.85,"conflict_note":"The exception is worded 'two- or three-unit owner-occupied premises with two (2) or fewer rental units', which is ambiguous. Coverage logic uses units <= 3 and owner_occupied."}],"notes":"Part 3 of 4, mostly habitability, receivership, lead paint, water testing and eviction procedure, which are out of scope. The only in-scope rule is the Anti-Eviction Act. The page mentions rent increases only in the context of the eviction ground for failure to pay an unconscionable or non-compliant increase, and states no rent-control coverage or cap, so no rent_increase_limits record was created. Effective and enacted dates are not stated in this part."}
